      "source": [
        "print(\"## Summary of Key Findings\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n### 1. Descriptive Statistics and Comparison of Means\")\n",
        "print(\"Comparing the descriptive statistics and mean values for Tamale and Kumasi reveals significant differences in several key environmental parameters:\")\n",
        "display(comparison_mean)\n",
        "print(\"\\n- **Soil Moisture:** Kumasi generally exhibits higher mean volumetric soil water moisture content across all three crops (tomato, pepper, eggplant) compared to Tamale, suggesting a potentially wetter environment in Kumasi.\")\n",
        "print(\"- **Soil Temperature:** Kumasi shows consistently higher mean soil temperatures for all three crops than Tamale.\")\n",
        "print(\"- **Solar Radiation:** Tamale has a higher mean PV solar radiation compared to Kumasi.\")\n",
        "print(\"- **Relative Humidity:** Kumasi has significantly higher mean relative humidity than Tamale.\")\n",
        "print(\"- **Air Temperature:** Tamale has a higher mean air temperature than Kumasi.\")\n",
        "print(\"- **Precipitation:** Both locations show very low mean precipitation during the study period, with Tamale having a slightly higher mean.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n### 2. Diurnal and Seasonal Patterns\")\n",
        "print(\"Analyzing the diurnal and seasonal patterns provides insights into the temporal variations in environmental conditions:\")\n",
        "print(\"\\n#### Diurnal Patterns (Hourly Averages):\")\n",
        "print(\"- **Temperature and Solar Radiation:** Both locations show typical diurnal patterns with temperatures and solar radiation peaking during the daytime hours and lowest at night.\")\n",
        "print(\"- **Relative Humidity:** Relative humidity generally follows an inverse diurnal pattern to temperature, being highest at night and lowest during the day.\")\n",
        "print(\"- **Soil Moisture and Temperature:** Soil moisture and temperature also exhibit diurnal cycles, influenced by air temperature, solar radiation, and potentially irrigation/precipitation events.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n#### Seasonal Patterns (Monthly Averages):\")\n",
