        "### Identify Extreme Outliers\n",
        "\n",
        "Subtask: Define a method for identifying extreme outliers and apply it to the relevant environmental parameters in both dataframes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Reasoning: To generate a statistical table on extreme outliers, I first need to identify which data points qualify as extreme outliers based on a defined statistical criterion. Using the Interquartile Range (IQR) is a common method for this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "0a75d7bc",
        "outputId": "d0f25538-e4f1-4576-faed-1e84124eabdb"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Function to identify extreme outliers using IQR\n",
        "def identify_extreme_outliers(df, column):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Identifies extreme outliers in a DataFrame column using the IQR method.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Args:\n",
        "        df (pd.DataFrame): The input DataFrame.\n",
        "        column (str): The name of the column to analyze.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        pd.Series: A boolean Series indicating whether each data point in the column is an extreme outlier.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Q1 = df[column].quantile(0.25)\n",
        "    Q3 = df[column].quantile(0.75)\n",
        "    IQR = Q3 - Q1\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Extreme outliers are typically defined as points outside 3 * IQR from Q1 or Q3\n",
        "    lower_bound = Q1 - 3 * IQR\n",
        "    upper_bound = Q3 + 3 * IQR\n",
        "\n",
        "    outliers = (df[column] < lower_bound) | (df[column] > upper_bound)\n",
        "    return outliers\n",
        "\n",
        "# Identify extreme outliers in key environmental parameters for both dataframes\n",
        "# We will use the same key_params that were used for the descriptive statistics and correlation analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "extreme_outliers_tamale = pd.DataFrame(index=df_tamale.index)\n",
        "extreme_outliers_kumasi = pd.DataFrame(index=df_kumasi.index)\n",
        "\n",
        "for param in key_params:\n",
        "    if param in df_tamale.columns:\n",
        "        extreme_outliers_tamale[param] = identify_extreme_outliers(df_tamale, param)\n",
        "    if param in df_kumasi.columns:\n",
        "         extreme_outliers_kumasi[param] = identify_extreme_outliers(df_kumasi, param)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Extreme outliers identified for key environmental parameters.\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Extreme outliers identified for key environmental parameters.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
